<main id="main">

<section class="pagehead">
  <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">English Literature · Notes</p>
    <h1>Literary Criticism</h1>
    <p class="lede">For more than two thousand years, thinkers have asked what literature is, what it is for and how it should be read. These notes gather their answers, section by section — the history of criticism, the main schools of theory, and the terms you need for your exams.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="border-top:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>History of Literary Criticism</h2>
    <p>Criticism in order of time, from the Greeks to about 1960. The series has two layers: first the period articles, then articles on the main critics of each period. Articles become clickable as each one is written.</p>
    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-introduction/">Introduction to Literary Criticism</a></h3>
        <p>What criticism is, what critics do, its main kinds, and a map of the whole history.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-classical/">Classical Criticism</a></h3>
        <p>Plato &middot; Aristotle &middot; Horace &middot; Longinus</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-renaissance/">Renaissance Criticism</a></h3>
        <p>Sidney &middot; Gosson &middot; Puttenham &middot; Jonson</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-neoclassical/">Neoclassical Criticism</a></h3>
        <p>Dryden &middot; Pope &middot; Addison &middot; Johnson</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-romantic/">Romantic Criticism</a></h3>
        <p>Wordsworth &middot; Coleridge &middot; Shelley &middot; Hazlitt</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-victorian/">Victorian Criticism</a></h3>
        <p>Arnold &middot; Ruskin &middot; Pater &middot; Wilde</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-early-twentieth/">Early Twentieth Century</a></h3>
        <p>Bradley &middot; T. S. Eliot &middot; I. A. Richards</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="meta">Available now</p>
        <h3><a href="/notes/literary-criticism-mid-twentieth/">Mid Twentieth Century</a></h3>
        <p>Empson &middot; Leavis &middot; the New Critics &middot; Frye</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ltx" id="literary-theory" style="background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--cream),var(--bg));border-top:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Literary Theory</h2>
    <p>The modern schools that ask how a text and its meaning work. The series runs in eight parts, in a rough order of time and of argument: each part answers, or quarrels with, the one before it. Open a part to see its chapters.</p>
    <div class="grid ltx-cards">
      {%- for part in literaryTheory %}
      <a class="ltx-card" href="{{ part.href }}">
        {%- if part.picture %}
        <span class="ltx-thumb"><img src="{{ part.picture.src }}" srcset="{{ part.picture.small }} 240w, {{ part.picture.src }} 480w" sizes="(max-width: 559px) 84px, (max-width: 860px) calc((100vw - 72px) / 2 - 24px), (max-width: 1120px) calc((100vw - 72px) / 3 - 24px), 230px" alt="{{ part.picture.alt }}" width="480" height="300" loading="lazy"><span class="ltx-tag">Part {{ part.number }}</span></span>
        {%- else %}
        <span class="ltx-thumb ltx-thumb-plain" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ltx-fig">{{ part.number }}</span></span>
        {%- endif %}
        <span class="ltx-meta">{{ part.count }} chapters</span>
        <span class="ltx-name">{{ part.name }}</span>
        <span class="ltx-sum">{{ part.summary }}</span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="meta">{{ literaryTheoryTotals.parts }} parts &middot; {{ literaryTheoryTotals.chapters }} chapters planned{% if literaryTheoryTotals.live == 0 %} &middot; Articles coming soon{% endif %}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ltx" id="cultural-studies" style="border-top:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Cultural Studies</h2>
    <p>Culture itself as the subject, not only books: how the field began, the Birmingham school, ideology and hegemony, class and taste, popular culture, media and audiences, subculture, gender, race, and diaspora and globalisation. Open a part to see its chapters.</p>
    <div class="grid ltx-cards ltx-cards-3">
      {%- for part in culturalStudies %}
      <a class="ltx-card" href="{{ part.href }}">
        {%- if part.picture %}
        <span class="ltx-thumb"><img src="{{ part.picture.src }}" srcset="{{ part.picture.small }} 240w, {{ part.picture.src }} 480w" sizes="(max-width: 559px) 84px, (max-width: 860px) calc((100vw - 72px) / 2 - 24px), 310px" alt="{{ part.picture.alt }}" width="480" height="300" loading="lazy"><span class="ltx-tag">Part {{ part.number }}</span></span>
        {%- else %}
        <span class="ltx-thumb ltx-thumb-plain" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ltx-fig">{{ part.number }}</span></span>
        {%- endif %}
        <span class="ltx-meta">{{ part.count }} chapters</span>
        <span class="ltx-name">{{ part.name }}</span>
        <span class="ltx-sum">{{ part.summary }}</span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="meta">{{ culturalStudiesTotals.parts }} parts &middot; {{ culturalStudiesTotals.chapters }} chapters planned{% if culturalStudiesTotals.live == 0 %} &middot; Articles coming soon{% endif %}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--cream),var(--bg));border-top:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Indian Poetics</h2>
    <p>The classical Indian tradition of aesthetics — rasa, dhvani and the Sanskrit theorists of poetry and drama.</p>
    <p class="meta" style="margin-top:.75rem">Articles coming soon.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="border-top:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Key Terms &amp; Concepts</h2>
    <p>A plain-English glossary of the terms used across criticism and theory, from mimesis and catharsis to canon and close reading.</p>
    <p class="meta" style="margin-top:.75rem">Articles coming soon.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</main>

<footer class="site-footer"></footer>

</body>
</html>
